The quadratic equation is \(5x^2 - 20x + 18 = 0\).  
Using the quadratic formula \(x = \frac{-b \pm \sqrt{b^2 - 4ac}}{2a}\) with \(a = 5\), \(b = -20\), \(c = 18\):

\[
x = \frac{20 \pm \sqrt{(-20)^2 - 4 \cdot 5 \cdot 18}}{2 \cdot 5}
= \frac{20 \pm \sqrt{400 - 360}}{10}
= \frac{20 \pm \sqrt{40}}{10}
= \frac{20 \pm 2\sqrt{10}}{10}
= \frac{10 \pm \sqrt{10}}{5}.
\]

So the roots are  
\[
x = \frac{10 + \sqrt{10}}{5}, \quad x = \frac{10 - \sqrt{10}}{5}.
\]
